From: Jonas Meyer-Ohle <19151471+jonas-meyer@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] usb: gadget: f_fs: accept video class-specific descriptors

ffs_do_single_desc() accepts class-specific descriptors only for HID,
CCID and DFU. A USB Video Class function needs CS_INTERFACE descriptors
(video control header, terminals, video streaming header, formats and
frames) and can have CS_ENDPOINT descriptors. f_fs rejects them with
-EINVAL, so userspace cannot implement a UVC function with FunctionFS.

Accept CS_INTERFACE and CS_ENDPOINT descriptors when the most recent
interface descriptor has the video class.

f_fs does not renumber the interface numbers and endpoint addresses in
these descriptors (baInterfaceNr of the video control header and
bEndpointAddress of the video streaming header). Userspace must write the
final values.

---
--- a/f_fs.c
+++ b/f_fs.c
@@ -2579,6 +2579,15 @@
 			return -EINVAL;
 		}
 
+	case USB_DT_CS_INTERFACE:
+	case USB_DT_CS_ENDPOINT:
+		if (*current_class != USB_CLASS_VIDEO) {
+			pr_vdebug("unknown descriptor: %d for class %d\n",
+				  _ds->bDescriptorType, *current_class);
+			return -EINVAL;
+		}
+		break;
+
 	case USB_DT_OTG:
 		if (length != sizeof(struct usb_otg_descriptor))
 			goto inv_length;
